# 🧩 STEP-BY-STEP: Auto-Download ChatGPT Files via Tampermonkey (Brave)

---

## 🐵 1. Install Tampermonkey in Brave

Tampermonkey is a popular user script manager.  
You’ll use it to run JavaScript that watches ChatGPT and downloads files as they appear.

👉 Click to install:  
🔗 [**Tampermonkey for Brave (Chrome Web Store)**](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/tampermonkey/dhdgffkkebhmkfjojejmpbldmpobfkfo)

Click **"Add to Brave"** → **"Add Extension"**

---

## 🧾 2. Create a New Userscript

Once installed:

1. Click the **Tampermonkey icon** (🦧) in the top-right corner of Brave
2. Click **"Create a new script"**
3. **Delete everything** in the editor

---

## 📥 3. Paste This Auto-Download Script

Paste this code into the blank editor:

```javascript
// ==UserScript==
// @name         Auto-Download ChatGPT Files
// @namespace    https://chat.openai.com
// @version      1.0
// @description  Automatically downloads files shared in ChatGPT
// @author       E.Apotheosis + AI CoPilot
// @match        https://chat.openai.com/*
// @grant        GM_download
// @run-at       document-end
// ==/UserScript==

(function() {
    'use strict';
    const downloaded = new Set();

    setInterval(() => {
        document.querySelectorAll('a').forEach(link => {
            const href = link.getAttribute('href');
            if (href && href.startsWith('sandbox:/mnt/data/') && !downloaded.has(href)) {
                const filename = href.split('/').pop();
                GM_download({ url: href, name: filename });
                downloaded.add(href);
                console.log(`Auto-downloading: ${filename}`);
            }
        });
    }, 2000); // check every 2 seconds
})();
```

---

## 💾 4. Save the Script

- Click **File** > **Save** (or hit `Ctrl+S`)
- You should now see **Auto-Download ChatGPT Files** listed in your Tampermonkey dashboard

---

## ✅ 5. Test It

1. Open [https://chat.openai.com](https://chat.openai.com)
2. Find a recent message from me that contains a download link (like `.md`, `.json`, etc)
3. If the script is working, it will **automatically download the file within 2 seconds**  
4. Check your `Downloads` folder — the file should be there 💾

---

## ⚙️ Optional: Customize Folder or Filename

Unfortunately, browsers limit userscripts from picking exact download *folders* for security reasons.

To control where they go:
- Set your browser’s **auto-download folder** in Brave settings  
- Or use a file-watching script to **move them into `/NYRA_Logs/`**, etc.

